-- title:
--   Ordinary line at λ exactly dividing the level, a_λ=±1
-- statement:
--   Let $M\ge 1$ and let $g$ be a weight-two cusp form on $\Gamma_0(M)$ which is a newform in the project's sense: $g$ is a normalised eigenform (its $q$-expansion coefficients satisfy $a_1=1$, multiplicativity at coprime indices, and the recursions $a_{p^{r+2}}=a_pa_{p^{r+1}}-p\,a_{p^r}$ for primes $p\nmid M$ and $a_{p^{r+2}}=a_pa_{p^{r+1}}$ for $p\mid M$), and for no proper divisor $M'\mid M$ is there a normalised eigenform of level $M'$ whose coefficients at primes not dividing $M$ agree with those of $g$. Let $\lambda$ be a prime, $S$ a finite set of naturals containing $\lambda$ and every prime divisor of $M$, and $O'$ a characteristic-zero adically complete discrete valuation domain with finite residue field in which $\lambda$ lies in the maximal ideal. Let $\chi_g$ be a ring homomorphism to $\mathbb{C}$ from the Hecke algebra of level $M$ and weight two away from $S\setminus\{\lambda\}$ (the $\mathbb{Z}$-subalgebra of $\mathrm{End}_{\mathbb{C}}$ of the cusp forms generated by the $T_\ell$ for primes $\ell\nmid M$ outside $S\setminus\{\lambda\}$ and the $U_q$ for primes $q\mid M$ outside it) with $\chi_g(T_\ell)=a_\ell(g)$ for all such $\ell$, and let $\iota$ be a ring homomorphism from the image of $\chi_g$ to $O'$. Let $\rho$ be an adic Galois representation over $O'$, i.e. a free $O'$-module $V$ of rank two with a multiplicative action of $\mathrm{Aut}_{\mathbb{Q}}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}})$ that is continuous for the adic filtration, such that for every prime $\ell\nmid M$ outside $S$, every valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $\ell$ a non-unit of $A$ and every $\sigma$ that is a Frobenius at $A$ for $\ell$ (lying in the decomposition group and inducing $x\mapsto x^\ell$ on the residue field), the characteristic polynomial of $\rho(\sigma)$ is $X^2-\iota(\chi_g(T_\ell))X+\ell$; assume the residual representation $\mathrm{ResidueField}(O')\otimes_{O'}V$ is absolutely irreducible. Assume $\lambda\mid M$ and $\lambda^2\nmid M$, and let $P$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $\lambda$ a non-unit of $P$. Then there are a submodule $L\subseteq V$ and an integer $a$ with $a=1$ or $a=-1$ such that $a_\lambda(g)=a$ in $\mathbb{C}$; $L=O'\cdot b_0$ for some $O'$-basis $(b_0,b_1)$ of $V$; $L$ is stable under every element of the decomposition subgroup of $P$ over $\mathbb{Q}$; $\rho(\tau)v-v\in L$ for every $\tau$ in the image of the inertia subgroup of $P$ and every $v\in V$; and $\rho(\sigma)v-a\,v\in L$ for every Frobenius $\sigma$ at $P$ for $\lambda$ and every $v\in V$.
--
--   This is the local–global compatibility at the residue characteristic for the $\lambda$-adic representation of a weight-two newform whose level is exactly divisible by $\lambda$: the representation is ordinary at $\lambda$, the stable line being the ramified part, with unramified quotient on which Frobenius acts by $a_\lambda(g)=\pm1$. It is used in the analysis of the local Hecke algebra at $\lambda$, where ordinarity is compared with the unit root and with the non-unit case of $a_\lambda$.
